Z||000007||GodSend||09-01-2000||11:11 AM||||  It looks pretty rough, buts its just the concept.  Heres a suggestion I would like to see...<P>  Before my Fiero I owned a Talon.  One thing I always loved about the Talon body was the Timing Belt Hump on the drivers side hood.  Its slightly off center, can it looks really nice from the outside and from the inside looking out.<P>  Seeing a fiero with something similar would look great.||||reg||1
Z||000008||Monkeyman||09-01-2000||11:45 AM||||I had a mid-'80s Buick Skyhawk (Cav brother).  It had the same hump, but mine was for the MC reservoir.  Some had a hump on both sides to clear the strut towers.  They do look nice if they're not excessively large.||||reg||1
Z||000009||mrfixit58||09-01-2000||02:48 PM||||Take another look. Keep in mind that the factory mounting studs are still in the scoop and making it look taller than is really is. The scoop itself is only about 1 1/2 inches tall. The vent can easily be opened for more ventilation and the scoop fits the contour of the hood pretty well. I dunno... it was just an idea. Maybe I'll buy a can of paint simular to my GT and remove the studs and take another look. If I do, I'll post more pics.<P>Roy  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><BR>||||reg||2
